    "details": "The rabbitmq-c project reports:\n\n> CVE-2026-44236: A malicious AMQP server can send an undersized\n> connection.tune.frame_max value during the login handshake. The\n> library does not enforce the protocol minimum frame size, reallocates\n> its outbound buffer to an invalid size and then writes frame data\n> beyond it, causing a heap buffer overflow before authentication\n> completes.\n>\n> CVE-2026-44235: An unsigned integer underflow in the frame length\n> computation when parsing undersized AMQP frames bypasses bounds checks\n> in the property and table decoders, leading to an out-of-bounds read\n> and client-side denial of service.\n",
    "id": "FreeBSD-2026-0496",
